# Normalise line endings in the working tree.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. `plugins/cds-theme` commits a BUILD ARTIFACT
# (`client/client.js`) and `npm test` starts with a freshness check that rebuilds
# the artifact and compares it byte for byte. With git's Windows default
# (`core.autocrlf=true`) a fresh clone checks the sources out with CRLF endings,
# esbuild then emits those CRLF sequences into string literals in the bundle, and
# the committed artifact — built with LF — no longer matches. The check fails for
# every Windows clone even though nothing is actually stale: measured at 83 extra
# bytes, exactly one per line ending that reached the bundle.
#
# Pinning `eol=lf` in the repository makes the working tree identical on every
# platform, so the artifact rebuilt from a clean checkout is byte-identical to the
# committed one. It also keeps the diff of a re-built artifact meaningful instead
# of "every line changed".
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch their bytes, never diff them.
*.woff2 binary
*.woff binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
